==============================================================================
ADJUDICATION: bare (active-coord Q) vs zero-padded (measure K) -- support-3 relations
==============================================================================
Canon THM-538 (CORRECTED): K(1,1,-1,0,0,0,0)=+0.00066 != 0  (a support-3 relation, k=8).

  Schur (1,1,-1) : bare=-0.000000  +3zeros(len6)=+0.000332  +4zeros(len7)=+0.000664  +5zeros(len8)=+0.000830
  3-AP  (1,-2,1) : bare=+0.000000  +3zeros(len6)=+0.000332  +4zeros(len7)=+0.000830  +5zeros(len8)=+0.001305
  supp2 (1,-1)x  : bare=+0.000000  +3zeros(len5)=+0.000000  +4zeros(len6)=-0.000953  +5zeros(len7)=-0.002860

VERDICT:
 * BARE vector  -> K=0 for support<=5  == the active-coord sum Q (HAS the support-6 floor).
 * ZERO-PADDED  -> K!=0 once total length>=6  == the MEASURE kernel (NO floor; canon THM-538).
 * corr(E)=Sum over Lambda°(E) uses ZERO-PADDED length-k vectors, so support-3 relations
   DO contribute (~+0.0007..0.0013 each at k=8). The AP, rich in support-3 relations
   (3-APs+Schur=additive energy A3), is support-3-dominated -> corr~0.30. HYP-2724 (A3 the
   driver, Pearson(A3,corr)=+0.93) STANDS; the workflow's 'support-6 carrier' is the
   conceded Q-vs-K conflation (THM-538 / MISTAKE-078).
